Package: texas2step
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Robert Patrick <193846785+robert-patrick-texas@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= @PYVER@), python3 (<< @PYNEXT@), libc6 (>= @GLIBC@), adduser
Recommends: nginx
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/robert-patrick-texas/texas2step
Description: browser-based throughput, latency, jitter and packet-loss tests
 texas2step serves a web page and REST API that measure the network path
 between a browser and this server: multi-stream HTTP throughput, latency and
 jitter idle and under load, and UDP packet loss over WebRTC.
 .
 This package installs a self-contained Python environment under
 /opt/texas2step, a systemd service on 127.0.0.1:8080, and nginx snippets
 that publish the service at /texas2step/ on an existing site.
